{"data":{"attachmentkeynames":["rs"],"desc":"Compose ONE commit message for ONE change group in a repo - READ-ONLY, stages/commits nothing. A group is what dev.git.store_status reports under one key: a store unit (lib.ctl), a library (lib), or any label for a set of plain files. `changes` is the group's item list [{state, what, path}] (a JSONArray; pass [] to have the unit looked up in store_status). The diff is taken over exactly those paths - not the whole library - so the message describes this group and is correct no matter WHO edited (agent, peer, MCP, or hand). Prompt = recent house-style subjects + sibling groups in the same batch + the changed-path listing + the capped diff. Enforces the contract: subject <=72 chars imperative, blank line, 1-4 why-bullets, an Agent-Message trailer. Falls back to a deterministic mechanical message when the LLM fails or misbehaves, so the caller can always commit. Makes exactly one LLM call. Returns {message, source:\"llm\"|\"fallback\", unit, paths}.","import":"use ndata::dataobject::DataObject;\nuse ndata::dataarray::DataArray;\nuse ndata::data::Data;\nuse crate::agent::llm::ask_llm::ask_llm;","params":[{"name":"repo","type":"String"},{"name":"unit","type":"String"},{"name":"siblings","type":"String"},{"name":"changes","type":"JSONArray"}],"returntype":"FLAT","type":"rust"},"id":"stxkgw1a101903675m1a7c","readers":[],"time":1794329349912,"username":"system","writers":[]}